    # If condition holds, on units modulo N the map is x -> x^N = x^(N-1+1),
    # so iterating corresponds to exponentiation by N on the unit group.
    # Need minimal k such that N^k ≡ 1 (mod ord(g)) for every unit g,
    # equivalently modulo λ(N), i.e. multiplicative order of N modulo λ(N).
    lam = carmichael_from_factorization(facN)

    # Since gcd(N, λ(N)) = 1 under the existence condition, order exists.
    if lam == 1:
        print(1)
